{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "עליה בחייה", :translit "aleha bechayyot", :gloss "to her, in her lifetime"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "עליה בחייה", :b "היבמה"}], :frame {:text "The phrase עליה בחייה concludes the verse Leviticus 18:18, which prohibits taking a woman together with her sister during the first sister's lifetime. The Ba'al HaTurim uses gematria to signal a branch of halakhic discussion: while the verse reads as a blanket prohibition on sisters, the law of yibum (levirate marriage) permits a man to marry his deceased brother's wife even when she is his wife's sister. The gematria thus compresses the tension between the plain prohibition and the exception carved out by the law of the yevamah.", :sources ["Leviticus 18:18" "Deuteronomy 25:5"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "עליה בחייה", :a-value 150, :b "היבמה", :b-value 62, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:23:59.355281025Z", :model "glm-5.2"}